          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can help, but it is not the most efficient choice. Standard hemp powder gives about 15 g of protein per 30 g serving, with lysine as its limiting amino acid and modest leucine. You need about 50 g of powder for 25 g of protein. For muscle, pea or soy isolate is denser; hemp works best mixed with them or inside a protein-rich meal."
