            "text": "For most healthy adults, a serving or two a day of a reputable hemp protein is a reasonable food. Because hemp can take up metals from soil, choose brands that share testing, rotate protein sources and avoid very high daily intakes. People with digestive conditions, kidney disease, pregnancy, allergies or regular medication should ask a doctor or registered dietitian first. This is not medical advice."
          }
        }
